== A. ring or ideal class: G_d = L_d u ((1+sqrt-d)/2 + L_d), odd squarefree d <= 199
  G_d is a ring exactly for d = 3 mod 4 (checked every odd squarefree d <= 199); for each of the 39 d = 1 mod 4 the checkerboard 2G_d = (2, 1+sqrt-d) is an ideal of L_d with square (2), principal only at d = 1
== B. the two grids are the whole class group
