== D. which grid carries a norm shell
  Z[omega], n <= 20000: odd shells split first : centred = 1 : 2 exactly; even shells lie on the first grid (r = 6 sum chi_-3 checked to 3000)
  Hurwitz order, n <= 300: odd n: Lipschitz 8 sigma(n), centred 16 sigma(n); even n: Lipschitz 24 sigma(odd part), centred 0
  d = 7 mod 8 ([7, 15, 23, 31, 39, 47]): every odd shell n <= 3000 lies on the first grid
  d = 11 (= 3 mod 8): every split-prime shell p < 3*10^5 lies on one grid; first grid for 4310 of 12963 = 0.3325 (Chebotarev in the cubic ring class field: 1/3)
  d = 19 (= 3 mod 8): every split-prime shell p < 3*10^5 lies on one grid; first grid for 4321 of 12959 = 0.3334 (Chebotarev in the cubic ring class field: 1/3)
  d = 43 (= 3 mod 8): every split-prime shell p < 3*10^5 lies on one grid; first grid for 4350 of 13011 = 0.3343 (Chebotarev in the cubic ring class field: 1/3)
  d = 67 (= 3 mod 8): every split-prime shell p < 3*10^5 lies on one grid; first grid for 4313 of 12927 = 0.3336 (Chebotarev in the cubic ring class field: 1/3)
  h(-4d)/h(-d) for squarefree d = 3 mod 4 below 200: 1 at d = 3, 3 for d = 3 mod 8 (d > 3), 1 for d = 7 mod 8 (42 values checked)
